    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change implements idempotent owner creation: when `POST /api/owners` repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, it returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate.\n\n### Approach \u2014 one new small file, nothing else touched\n\nI added a single self-contained controller, `OwnerIdempotentCreateControllerV1`, rather than editing the existing `addOwner` method. Key points:\n\n- **Mapping by specificity**: it maps `POST /api/owners` with `headers = \"Idempotency-Key\"`. Spring picks this more-specific mapping only when the header is present; requests without the header still hit the original generated `addOwner` path unchanged. No routing conflict, no change to existing behaviour.\n- **Reuse, not duplication**: it injects the existing `OwnerRestControllerV1` and delegates the real creation to its `addOwner`, so all the business-rule policies (postcode, quota, household, customer-code, audit, etc.) run exactly as before on the first request.\n- **Idempotency store**: a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, OwnerDto>` keyed by the header. First key \u2192 delegate, store the result, return its 201. Repeated key \u2192 short-circuit before any duplicate check and return the stored owner with 200 (avoiding the 409 the duplicate policy would otherwise raise).\n\n### Structural impact\n\n- **Files touched: 1** (a new file; no existing method modified).\n- The changed function has **CC \u2248 2** (one `if`) and **WMC_other = 0** (it's the only method in its class), so the cost formula `max(WMC_other,1) * CC * changed_lines` stays minimal \u2014 the expensive `addOwner` method inside the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` class is never edited.",
