    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered chain for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Routing note\nTwo controllers map `POST /api/owners`:\n- **`OwnerIdempotentCreateControllerV1`** wins only when an `Idempotency-Key` header is present. It short-circuits with `200 OK` + the stored DTO if that key was seen before; otherwise it delegates to the ordinary `addOwner` below (and caches the result under the key).\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** is the ordinary path \u2014 everything below happens here.\n\n## Ordered validations & side-effects\n\n**1. Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` gate before the method runs.\n\n**2. Bean Validation** of the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (from `OwnerFieldsDto`; `400` on failure):\n- `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/'/- separated parts)\n- `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, optional trailing `.`)\n- `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (must contain non-whitespace)\n- `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (exactly 10 digits, non-digits allowed between)\n- `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n- `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern` (exactly 4 digits)\n- `title`/`address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`: `@Size(max)` bounds\n\n**3. DTO \u2192 Owner mapping** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, normalizing side-effects):\n- `id` and `pets` ignored\n- `address` composed \u2014 prefers `addressLine1` (+ `addressLine2` after a space) over the flat `address`; the chosen value is normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`)\n- `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` normalized the same way\n- `telephone` normalized to E.164 (`E164Telephone.toE164`)\n- `email` lower-cased\n\n**4. `OwnerRegistrationDatePolicy.assignBusinessDayRegistrationDate`**\n- rejects a supplied registration date later than today (`400`)\n- defaults to server's current date when none supplied\n- rolls Saturday/Sunday/public-holiday forward to the next business day, then sets `registrationDate`\n\n**5. `OwnerDailyLimitPolicy.rejectWhenDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 counts existing owners sharing that (business-day) `registrationDate`; rejects if \u2265 100 (`429`).\n\n**6. `OwnerCityCapacityPolicy.rejectWhenCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 if `city` non-null, counts existing owners in that city; rejects if \u2265 50 (`409`).\n\n**7. `OwnerPostcodePolicy.rejectInvalidPostcode`** \u2014 if `postcode` present *and* city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), rejects when out of that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) (`400`). Missing postcode or unknown-region city passes.\n\n**8. `OwnerDisposableEmailPolicy.rejectDisposableDomain`** \u2014 if `email` present and contains `@`, rejects when the domain is on the blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) (`400`).\n\n**9. `OwnerHouseholdPolicy.rejectDuplicateHousehold`** \u2014 always sets `householdId` (first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`); then, if another existing owner shares the same (normalized last name, postcode) household, rejects unless `sharesHousehold == true` (`409`). The id is assigned either way.\n\n**10. `OwnerNamesakePolicy.assignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**11. `OwnerCustomerCodePolicy.assignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (REGION from postcode range else `UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`), de-duplicated by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 against existing codes.\n\n**12. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persists via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns the DB id).\n\n**13. `OwnerAuditPolicy.auditCreate`** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n**14. Response construction** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived read-only fields for the body (`displayName`, `telephoneDisplay`, `checkDigit`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `timezone`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, `ageBand`, `selfLink` \u2014 these are *not* persisted), sets the `Location` header, and returns `201 CREATED`.\n\n## Notes\n- Steps 4\u201311 run in exactly that source order and each can short-circuit the request with the status shown.\n- The many other `Owner*Policy` classes (telephone-length, check-digit, age-band, timezone, locality, membership, etc.) are **not** invoked in the create path itself \u2014 they're only used as read-side derivations in step 14's DTO mapping (or unused here).\n- The plain create path is not `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), so these steps are not wrapped in a single transaction."
